# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ask Juice Doctor AI — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. Secrets are server-only and
# must never be committed. The app degrades to an honest "unavailable" state
# when a provider is not configured — it never fabricates AI answers or data.
#
# Every variable listed here is read by the codebase (src/lib/env.ts and the
# Supabase clients). Integrations that are not yet implemented (email provider,
# payments, voice, monitoring, live Thryve, vector embeddings) have NO
# variables — none are listed until the integration actually exists.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ══ REQUIRED for the live platform ═══════════════════════════════════════════

# Supabase (database + auth). URL + anon key are PUBLIC (safe in the browser);
# the service-role key is SERVER-ONLY (bypasses RLS) — never expose it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Anthropic Claude — powers the receptionist assessment, all specialist
# replies and the admin playground. SERVER-ONLY. Without it, AI features show
# an honest "AI unavailable" state.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Base URL for auth redirects (password reset links, post-login continue).
# Set to the deployed origin in production; defaults to http://localhost:3011.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ══ OPTIONAL — tuning & behaviour ════════════════════════════════════════════

# AI provider + model. Only "anthropic" is implemented; the provider
# abstraction lets another be added without rewriting the HERNE engine.
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Default model (preferred over the legacy AI_MODEL, which is still honoured).
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Guardrails on every live call + durable per-user usage limits.
AI_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=14000
AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1024
# Request timeout: milliseconds (>=1000) or seconds (<1000, scaled up).
AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=60000
AI_DAILY_USER_LIMIT=50
AI_MONTHLY_USER_LIMIT=500

# Reserved seam (src/services/index.ts): setting APP_MODE=production selects
# database-backed marketing-content providers once client-approved copy moves
# into the database. Leave unset until then — unset keeps the file-based
# placeholder marketing content (pending client-supplied copy). Never gate
# secrets on this.
# APP_MODE=production

# ── Wearables (Thryve) — read by src/services/herne/wearable/provider.ts ─────
# The wearable architecture (consent, ingest engine, webhook endpoint at
# /api/webhooks/thryve, disconnect-with-deletion) is live but INERT until all
# three are set — until then connections are honestly unavailable and the
# webhook answers 503. Supplied by the client with the Thryve contract.
# THRYVE_API_KEY=
# THRYVE_APP_ID=
# THRYVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ══ TOOLING ONLY (not runtime) ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

# Supabase Management API token (sbp_…) + project ref — used by migration and
# key-management tooling, never by the running app.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=
